  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nDaily shower and thunderstorm chances are in place through the week.\nWith multiple rounds of precipitation expected, will have to \nwatch for additional flooding potential. Flood watch remains in\neffect for thunderstorms this afternoon across portions of central\nOhio down through the Scioto River Valley and portions of northern\nKentucky. Held off on potential new flood watch for Sunday until\ndetails can be resolved and current thunderstorms move out of the\narea. Still a small chance for an isolated strong to severe storm\nacross far eastern portions of the region into the evening hours.\n\nLooking at the remainder of the week, there will be daily chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms across the region. Not every location will\nbe under the potential for thunderstorms each day however.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nWhile temperatures will be slightly above or below normal at times,\nin general expect temperatures to be near normal values this week.",
